---
// "How we measure" for the done-for-you offer. Shared by /done-for-you/ and its industry pages.
---
<section class="dfy-measure" aria-labelledby="measure-heading">
  <h2 id="measure-heading">How we measure</h2>
  <p class="dfy-measure-lead">The result is defined before we start, from your own phone and booking records.</p>
  <dl class="record">
    <div>
      <dt>Baseline</dt>
      <dd>The 14 days before go-live, from your phone system's call log: (a) inbound calls during the hours the receptionist will cover, (b) how many were answered or got a usable message (caller name, reason and callback number), which we call "captured", and (c) appointments booked by phone, from your booking system.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Measurement window</dt>
      <dd>Days 31 to 60 after go-live, once tuning has settled. Same hours, same sources.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd>
        Either of these:
        <ul class="dfy-either">
          <li>At least <strong>90% of inbound calls</strong> in covered hours are captured (answered, booked, transferred, or a usable message taken), <strong>or</strong></li>
          <li>Phone-booked appointments are at least <strong>15% higher per week</strong> than the baseline weekly average.</li>
        </ul>
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
